(task (id "b09507db") (title "Keep ordinary comments, so the codebase can be the source of truth for the toolchain") (state "done") (priority 2) (assignee "") (labels "dogfood" "design") (parent "") (details "Only doc comments survive add; the -- comments that explain why are lost, so deus/*.deus cannot yet be regenerated from the codebase. Store them as metadata and print them back.") (links (change "c1f5fb9764e8d7266377799df31551052dfa205adbcb1f0245b9bdd239994b53")) (comments (comment "claude" "Design question before building: storing each definition's source text in its metadata keeps comments, but that text depends on its file's namespace and open lines, and goes stale when a dependency is renamed. A workable rule: print the stored text only while every name in it still resolves to the hash it had when added, and keep namespace and opens with it; otherwise print from Core as now.") (comment "claude" "Written up as P8 in docs/PROPOSALS.md, four options; recommending B (source text as metadata while it still resolves, export rebuilds the files). Waiting on a choice before building.") (comment "claude" "Character literals are lost too: '\"' is stored and printed as 34. Source text as metadata (P8 B) would keep both.") (comment "claude" "Built as comments on Core, the user's choice (D66): lead and notes metadata, restored by the printer. Character literals still print as numbers; filed separately.")))
